## ViewModel / Response DTO Pattern

All response types for API endpoints are defined in the usecase layer and returned directly by usecase methods.

### File Organization:

```
internal/usecase/[feature]/
├── viewmodels.go           # All response types for this feature
├── usecase.go              # Main usecase struct
├── usecase_[action].go     # Usecase methods returning ViewModels
└── [specific].go           # Other files
```

### ViewModel Definition Example:

```go
// internal/usecase/event/viewmodels.go
package event

import (
    "time"
    "github.com/google/uuid"
    "apps/backend/core-api/internal/entity"
)

// EventResponse - returned by event list and detail endpoints
type EventResponse struct {
    ID                       uuid.UUID          `json:"id"`
    ChainID                  int32              `json:"chain_id"`
    Title                    string             `json:"title"`
    ShortDescription         string             `json:"short_description"`
    LongDescription          string             `json:"long_description"`
    StartDate                time.Time          `json:"start_date"`
    EndDate                  time.Time          `json:"end_date"`
    Location                 string             `json:"location"`
    MaxAttendees             int32              `json:"max_attendees"`
    IsPublic                 bool               `json:"is_public"`
    IsVerified               bool               `json:"is_verified"`
    BannerPresignedURL       string             `json:"banner_presigned_url"`
    IconPresignedURL         string             `json:"icon_presigned_url"`
    CreatedAt                time.Time          `json:"created_at"`
    UpdatedAt                time.Time          `json:"updated_at"`
    EventStatus              entity.EventStatus `json:"event_status"`
}

// GetEventListViewModel - wrapper for list responses
type GetEventListViewModel struct {
    Events    []EventResponse `json:"events"`
    Total     int32           `json:"total"`
    Page      int32           `json:"page"`
    PageSize  int32           `json:"page_size"`
}
```

### Usecase Returning ViewModel:

```go
// internal/usecase/event/usecase_get_event.go
func (uc *EventUseCase) GetEventByID(ctx context.Context, eventID uuid.UUID, user *auth.JwtClaims) (*EventResponse, error) {
    // Business logic and data gathering
    event, err := uc.EventDg.GetEventByID(ctx, eventID)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }

    // Get presigned URLs (S3 service call)
    bannerURL, err := uc.S3Service.GetPresignedURL(ctx, event.BannerStorageKey)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }

    iconURL, err := uc.S3Service.GetPresignedURL(ctx, event.IconStorageKey)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }

    // Return fully constructed ViewModel
    return &EventResponse{
        ID:                 event.ID,
        ChainID:            int32(event.ChainId),
        Title:              event.Title,
        ShortDescription:   event.ShortDescription,
        LongDescription:    event.LongDescription,
        StartDate:          event.StartDate,
        EndDate:            event.EndDate,
        Location:           event.Location,
        MaxAttendees:       int32(event.MaxAttendees),
        IsPublic:           event.IsPublic,
        IsVerified:         event.IsVerified,
        BannerPresignedURL: bannerURL,
        IconPresignedURL:   iconURL,
        CreatedAt:          event.CreatedAt,
        UpdatedAt:          event.UpdatedAt,
        EventStatus:        event.EventStatus,
    }, nil
}
```

### Handler Using ViewModel:

```go
// internal/handler/event/get_event_by_id.go
// @Summary Get event by ID
// @Description Get event details by ID
// @Tags Events
// @ID get-event-by-id
// @Param event_id path string true "Event ID"
// @Success 200 {object} event.EventResponse
// @Router /api/v1/events/{event_id} [get]
func (h *Handler) GetEventByID(ctx *fiber.Ctx) error {
    eventID, err := uuid.Parse(ctx.Params("event_id"))
    if err != nil {
        return customerror.Parse(&customerror.ErrInvalidArgument, err)
    }

    user, err := h.AuthService.GetUserContext(ctx)
    if err != nil {
        return customerror.Parse(&customerror.ErrUnauthorized, err)
    }

    // Usecase returns the ViewModel directly
    event, err := h.EventUc.GetEventByID(ctx.Context(), eventID, user)
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }

    if event == nil {
        return customerror.Parse(&customerror.ErrNotFound, nil)
    }

    // Handler returns ViewModel directly as JSON
    return ctx.Status(fiber.StatusOK).JSON(event)
}
```

### Benefits of Usecase-Level ViewModels:

- ✅ **Single Responsibility**: Usecase handles all data gathering and transformation
- ✅ **Reusable**: Multiple handlers can use the same ViewModel from the same usecase
- ✅ **Testable**: Easy to test usecase without handlers
- ✅ **Clear Contract**: ViewModels define the exact response structure
- ✅ **Clean Handlers**: Handlers just call usecase and return result

## File Naming Conventions

- Handlers: `handler_[action].go` (e.g., `handler_register_with_google_oauth.go`)
- UseCases: `usecase_[action].go` (e.g., `usecase_register_user.go`)
- Repositories: `repository_[action].go` (e.g., `repository_create_user.go`)
- ViewModels: `viewmodels.go` (one file per feature for all response types)
- Routes: `routes.go` (one per feature)
- Main struct: `handler.go`, `usecase.go`, `repository.go`

